# PSM train → eval → promote gate

Do **not** judge a checkpoint by `effective_stored` alone. That is a storage-decision
number on 10 hand-written fixtures — it does **not** prove memories are extractable,
retrievable, or useful. Every train run must produce a full case report **and** a real
ingestion + retrieval smoke on non-training data before the checkpoint is promoted.

## Hard rules

1. **Never gate on a single aggregate.** Report all layers, every run: storage decision,
   facts, memory content, temporal/indexables, retrieval.
2. **Never eval on training data.** Ingestion + retrieval smoke must run on a frozen
   holdout that is provably absent from every curriculum/DPO JSONL for that adapter line.
3. **Different questions than ingest.** Retrieval questions must not be the same rows used
   for labeling/DPO/curriculum.
4. **No blind training.** Do not launch another SFT/DPO sweep until the smoke gate below
   can run and produce numbers for the checkpoint under test.

## Post-train checklist (run every time, in order)

### A. Storage report — full case table (not just aggregate)
Per prod fixture case, record and actually review:
- `action` vs `expectAction`
- `parse_valid` / `fail_safe` / `repair_status`
- `memory.content` snippet
- `facts[]` count + grounded vs `keyTokens`
- `indexables[]` + temporal fields (flag when empty/missing — do not silently pass)
- guard route if rejected
Publish the case table; do not summarize to one number.

### B. Holdout ingestion smoke (non-training data)
- Frozen holdout: LoCoMo conversations held out by conv id (never in any curriculum for
  v5n+), or a synthetic pack of unseen assistant turns.
- Ingest through the **PSM CLI path** (`operation=remember_llm_response`,
  `conversation=[assistant]`) — same shape as prod.
- Assert: sane store rate, no JSON/curriculum bleed, stored text contains expected entities.

### C. Holdout retrieval smoke (different questions than ingest)
- Same holdout convs, a **different** QA subset than anything used to label/train.
- Small N (e.g. 2 convs, ~10 questions) so it runs fast every time.
- Metrics: `hit_at_1`, `answer_accuracy` (min bar: retrieved memory contains the evidence span).

### D. Artifacts + promote
- Upload adapter + metrics + all eval reports to HF; verify locally.
- **Promote only if:** storage case table is healthy **and** holdout retrieval does not
  regress vs the current best baseline (today: `hf-prod-v5n-dpo-qwen0.5b`).
- Only after upload+verify: stop the pod. Never delete before the checklist is complete.

## Known infra gaps (fix before trusting retrieval numbers)
- `answer-evaluate.ts` / `buildHfPsmRuntime` default to the **v5k two-pass** adapters
  (`hf-prod-v5k-gate-distill` + `hf-prod-v5k-extract`), not the current single-adapter
  JSON best (`v5n-dpo`). Point end-to-end eval at the checkpoint under test.
- `filter_locomo_holdout.py` exists but is **not** wired into the train pipeline — run it
  (or hold out whole convs) before building any LoCoMo-touching curriculum.
- No temporal/indexable metric exists yet — add expected-indexable holdout cases before
  claiming temporal quality.
- `v5h / v5k / v5l / v5m` trained on LoCoMo evidence turns → LoCoMo is **not** a clean
  holdout for those lines. `v5n / v5n-dpo` are conversation-only → LoCoMo is fair there.

## Deploy bar (real, not proxy)
Fixtures **≥7/10** effective_stored with a healthy case table **and** holdout retrieval
**≥ baseline**. `effective_stored` alone is never sufficient to ship.
